  "source": "data/vehicles/car_sedan_awd.json with the wheel positions and tyre size matched to the imported model data/models/imported/lct_3000/lct_3000.glb (tools/carimport): wheelbase 3.345 m (front axle 1.672 m ahead of the CoG, the base car's CoG fraction kept), track front 1.888 m / rear 1.762 m, tyre road 225/70 R16 (model wheel radius 0.357 m). Everything else is the base file's. Base source: Reference AWD variant of data/vehicles/car_sedan.json (owner request 2026-09-25: FWD/RWD/AWD reference cars as simple baselines; car_sedan.json = FWD reference, car_sedan_rwd.json = RWD reference). Identical to car_sedan_rwd.json (50/50 static split, wheel attachments on data/models/car_sedan/car_sedan.rig.json's susp_* pivots, springs/dampers/ARBs, tyres, engine, clutch, gearbox, brakes, aero, driver aids - see that file's own source field for every number) except the driveline: gearbox.out -> open centre differential (ratio 1.0, lossless, 50/50 torque split, carrier inertia 0.01 kg*m^2 - a plain bevel/planetary centre diff as in early permanent-AWD saloons) -> front and rear open axle differentials (final drive 4.06, efficiency 0.97, the same unit as the FWD/RWD variants so overall gearing is unchanged) -> all four hubs. No centre lock, viscous coupling or LSD: this is the simplest AWD baseline (an open centre diff lets one spinning wheel take all the drive, which is expected behaviour for this layout, not a bug). The rear-axle handbrake acts on RL/RR only, so on its own it holds the car only through the gearbox when a gear is engaged. Racing_game-owned copy (physics_sim is read-only from this repo): identical to external/physics_sim's data/vehicles/car_sedan_awd.json except (1) every relative file reference points back into external/physics_sim/data/ (this file lives in racing_game/data/vehicles/), and (2) engine garage G1 added a fuel_tank component (E5, 60 L = 44.99 kg capacity at 749.8 kg/m3, initial 48 L = 35.99 kg [AS], the hyper car's 75 L / 60 L ratio kept) and the engine.fuel fluid link, so the garage can offer the fuel choice (D1) on every catalog car. Engine thermal model (2026-10-12, owner decision: every game car has one): names external/physics_sim/data/cooling_systems/sedan.json (the passenger-car class radiator and fan) and starts warm (engine_thermal_start, coolant 91 C, oil 95 C); the engine file supplies the engine side via default_thermal. Tyres (2026-10-13, universal tyres): no tyre files - each wheel carries a tyre_spec (compound + width/aspect/rim) that rg::load_vehicle builds in memory from data/tyres/families.json (tyre_families); a raw ps::io::load_vehicle_json of this file is rejected (physics_sim 6c5bb87: a wheel without a tyre is a load error); rg::load_vehicle injects the tyres through VehicleLoadOptions::tyres.",
